<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-chile"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Chile.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Chile</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Augusto Pinochet’s coup overthrows Salvador Allende on 11 September</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/new-zealand"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Zealand.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Zealand</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Britain joins the EEC, ending New Zealand's secure British market</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-greece"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Greece.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Greece</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The junta abolishes the monarchy</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/united-kingdom"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/United%20Kingdom.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>United Kingdom</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The UK joins the European Economic Community</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/swazi-kingdom"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Swazi%20Kingdom.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Swazi Kingdom</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sobhuza II repeals the constitution and bans political parties</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/tanzania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tanzania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tanzania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Dodoma is designated the future capital</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/arabic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Arabic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Arabic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Arabic becomes an official language of the United Nations</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/norse-religion"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Norse%20religion.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Norse religion</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Iceland recognises the modern Ásatrú fellowship as a religion</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/dictatorship"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dictatorship.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dictatorship</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">General Augusto Pinochet’s coup overthrows Chile’s elected government</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/military-junta"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Military%20junta.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Military junta</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The commanders of Chile’s army, navy, air force and police seize power and rule as a junta until 1990</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/presidential-democracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Presidential%20democracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Presidential democracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Chile’s armed forces overthrow President Salvador Allende, ending four decades of constitutional rule</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/saudi-arabia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Saudi%20Arabia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Saudi Arabia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Saudi Arabia leads an oil embargo against the Western countries that supported Israel in the Yom Kippur War, and oil prices quadruple.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-egypt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Egypt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Egypt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sadat coordinates with Syria in the Fourth Arab-Israeli War to reclaim Sinai, restoring Arab morale and his own legitimacy.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/rwanda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rwanda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rwanda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Juvénal Habyarimana takes power in a military coup; pro-Hutu discrimination continues with less violence and more prosperity.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/oriental-republic-of-uruguay"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Oriental%20Republic%20of%20Uruguay.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Oriental Republic of Uruguay</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">At President Juan María Bordaberry's request the armed forces disband Parliament and establish a civilian-military regime.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/peronism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Peronism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Peronism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Perón returns from exile and is elected president again with 62% of the vote</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/tao-te-ching"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Tao%20Te%20Ching.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tao Te Ching</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Archaeologists recover the Mawangdui Silk Texts</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Paris Peace Accords are signed on 27 January, and US military forces leave South Vietnam at the end of March</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/dream-of-the-red-chamber"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dream%20of%20the%20Red%20Chamber.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dream of the Red Chamber</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">David Hawkes publishes the first volume of The Story of the Stone, the first eighty chapters in English for Penguin Classics</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/american-indian-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/American%20Indian%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>American Indian Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">About 300 Oglala Lakota and AIM activists occupy Wounded Knee, South Dakota, in a siege that lasts 71 days</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/ghost-dance"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ghost%20Dance.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ghost Dance</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lakota men and women, among them Mary Brave Bird, dance the Ghost Dance at Wounded Knee during the occupation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/black-consciousness-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Black%20Consciousness%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Black Consciousness Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The government begins to clamp down, and virtually the entire leadership of SASO and the Black Community Programmes is banned</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/neoliberalism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Neoliberalism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Neoliberalism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A coup in Chile establishes the military junta of Augusto Pinochet, which later adopts the Chicago Boys’ reforms</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/religion/ahmadiyya"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ahmadiyya.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ahmadiyya</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Organisation of Islamic Cooperation declares that the Ahmadiyya is not linked to Islam</span></li></ul></section>
